course: dictionary
lesson: 8272
title: Righteousness: doing what is right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Righteousness is a noun. It means being morally good, honest and fair, and doing what is right. When you read it, ask: what is the good thing being done here?
explain: In church and Bible lessons it has a special meaning: being right with God. «Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness» (Matthew 5) uses the word in this way. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Be careful with the warning in «Be careful not to practise your righteousness in front of others to be seen by them» (Matthew 6:1-4). The clue is «to be seen by them». Doing good to look good is not the point. Being honest about your reasons helps you do good for good reasons.
fact: Righteousness means being morally good, honest and fair; doing what is right.
fact: Righteousness is uncountable, so you say some righteousness, not a righteousness.
fact: In church lessons it can mean being right with God, which Christians believe comes through God's grace and faith.
fact: «Self-righteousness» means being too sure you are better than others.
fact: «Paths of righteousness» means the right and good ways to live.
exercise: «Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness.» What does righteousness mean here? | Winning every game | *Doing what is right and being good | Being very tired after a long day | Being good, honest and fair
exercise: A hero in a story fights for righteousness. What does this suggest? | Running away from danger | Fighting for a prize for himself | *Fighting for what is right, fair and just | Hiding in a cave
exercise: Which word means being too sure you are better than others? | *Self-righteousness | Honesty | Kindness | Fairness
test: «Be careful not to practise your righteousness in front of others to be seen by them.» Why does the author warn against this? | Because righteousness is only for grown-ups | *Because doing good just to be seen by others misses the point | Because righteousness is bad | Because others never notice good deeds
test: Which is the best example of righteousness? | Running fast in a race | *Returning a lost purse to its owner because it is the right thing to do | Painting a picture of the sea | Eating three cakes before dinner
exam: What part of speech is righteousness? | Adverb | *Noun | Preposition | Verb
